429-### D-42 · Two header types; logo only on home-base screens — 2026-10-14
430-- **Decision (Apurva):** the app has two header types, used by screen type.
431-  - **Home-base header** — logo on the left (D-02 lockup), actions on the right. Used on **sign-in** and **Home** (all its states).
432-  - **Task header** — Back + screen title, **no logo**. (2026-10-14: Back only where there is a previous screen — none on the faster sign-in offer or returning unlock, D-47; the case page's Back follows D-48; hero vs compact size, D-49.) Used on **OTP**, the **faster sign-in offer**, **returning unlock**, the **case page** and every other step or task screen.
433-- **Why:** consistency comes from a predictable header per screen type, not from repeating the logo. Sign-in needs the logo for trust before a doctor types their number; Home is the screen doctors return to all day. On step and task screens the space is worth more for the task (OTP fits above the keyboard only without the logo; the case page needs it for patient context).
434-- **Rejected:** logo on every screen (costs space where it's needed most); logo on no screen (loses trust on sign-in and identity on Home).
435-- **Changes:** D-33 "Look" — the blue band + white panel stays shared with OTP and returning unlock, but the logo no longer appears on those screens. D-02 (which lockup) unchanged.
