437-### D-43 · Screen layout and type scale — 2026-10-14
438-- **Decision (Apurva):** every mobile screen follows the central layout rules in `design-system/RULES.md` §8:
439-  - **Type scale, 4 levels:** L1 screen title 32/40 semibold · L2 key content 16/24 · L3 supporting 14/20 secondary colour · L4 fine print 12/16 secondary colour. Only the screen title is large; buttons keep their design-system style.
440-  - **Spacing:** one side margin (24) on every screen; only three gaps — tight 8 (label↔field, field↔helper), related 16 (within a group), section 32 (between groups). Spare space goes between content and a pinned button, never inside a group.
441-  - **Button placement:** on screens where the doctor types (sign-in, OTP), the main button sits **inline, directly under the content**, so it stays visible above the keyboard without moving. On screens without typing (faster sign-in offer, Home), the main button is **pinned to the bottom**.
442-- **Why:** spacing and text sizes had been set by eye per screen, so screens drifted and nothing led the eye. A pinned button on typing screens either jumps with the keyboard or leaves a gap above it (tested in concepts v2a).
443-- **Rejected:** pinned bottom button on sign-in/OTP; auto-opening the keyboard on sign-in (D-33 layout kept as approved).
