508-### D-48 · Leaving a case: Back by stage, end-of-case exits, "case" wording — 2026-10-14
509-- **Problem (Apurva):** once a doctor opens a case there is no way back to Home — the case page only moves forward, and "Next Order" chains case to case. Home now holds availability (time left, Add time, End availability), so the doctor must be able to reach it.
510-- **Decision (Apurva):** the case page has a **Back** in its header, and the phone's back gesture behaves the same. Back always means "leave this case"; the outcome depends on the stage:
511-
512-  | Stage | Back (header or phone gesture) |
513-  |---|---|
514-  | Case assigned, **no call attempted** | Confirmation sheet → **release the case** → Home |
515-  | Call **attempted or connected**, until the case is closed | **Blocked.** Header Back is hidden; the back gesture shows a calm, neutral message (not an error): "Finish this case first. Then you can go back to Home." |
516-  | **Case closed** | Straight to Home, no sheet |
517-
518-  - **Release only before the first attempted call.** Once a call is attempted (even if not connected), the case is closed through the flow (no pickup, callback, etc.), never released.
519-  - **Confirmation sheet:** title "Leave this case?" · text "It goes back to the queue for another doctor." · primary "Release case" · quiet "Stay on this case".
520-  - **End of a case:** primary **"Request next case"** + secondary **"Back to Home"**, stacked in the pinned bar (as on Home). The completion confirmation sits at the top of the content, medicines shown as prescribed, and its title names the path just taken (2026-10-14): **"Prescription confirmed"** (Cat4, HA skipped) · **"Transferred to HA"** (value meds) · **"Forwarded to HA"** (non-value meds). If availability ended during the case, only **"Back to Home"** (Home then shows the expired state; D-36: a case is never interrupted).
## 2n. Home round before the final deploy (Apurva, 2026-11-10) — final deploy on hold until this is done
